{"id":10101,"name":"sandshrew-alola","speciesId":27,"dex":27,"form":"alolan","generation":1,"types":["ice","steel"],"stats":{"hp":50,"attack":75,"defense":90,"special-attack":10,"special-defense":35,"speed":40},"abilities":[{"name":"snow-cloak","hidden":false},{"name":"slush-rush","hidden":true}],"height":7,"weight":400,"baseExp":60,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10101.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/10101.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/10101.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/10101.ogg","genus":"Mouse Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"Burrows deep underground in arid locations far from water. It only emerges to hunt for food."},{"version":"yellow","text":"Its body is dry. When it gets cold at night, its hide is said to become coated with a fine dew."},{"version":"gold","text":"If it fell from a great height, this POKéMON could save itself by rolling into a ball and bouncing."},{"version":"silver","text":"Disliking water, it lives in deep burrows in arid areas. It can roll itself instantly into a ball."},{"version":"crystal","text":"It prefers dry, sandy places because it uses the sand to protect itself when threatened."},{"version":"ruby","text":"SANDSHREW’s body is configured to absorb water without waste, enabling it to survive in an arid desert. This POKéMON curls up to protect itself from its enemies."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"SANDSHREW has a very dry hide that is extremely tough. The POKéMON can roll into a ball that repels any attack. At night, it burrows into the desert sand to sleep."},{"version":"emerald","text":"When it curls up in a ball, it can make any attack bounce off harmlessly. Its hide has turned tough and solid as a result of living in the desert."},{"version":"firered","text":"It burrows and lives underground. If threatened, it curls itself up into a ball for protection."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"Burrows deep underground in arid locations far from water. It only emerges to hunt for prey."},{"version":"diamond","text":"To protect itself from attackers, it curls up into a ball. It lives in arid regions with minimal rainfall."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"If it fell from a great height, this Pokémon could save itself by rolling into a ball and bouncing."},{"version":"black-2","text":"It digs deep burrows to live in. When in danger, it rolls up its body to withstand attacks."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Sandshrew’s body is configured to absorb water without waste, enabling it to survive in an arid desert. This Pokémon curls up to protect itself from its enemies."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Sandshrew has a very dry hide that is extremely tough. The Pokémon can roll into a ball that repels any attack. At night, it burrows into the desert sand to sleep."},{"version":"sun","text":"It can roll its body into a ball. It moves through the desert by rolling at high speeds."},{"version":"moon","text":"It usually makes its home in deserts and arid zones, where rain does not fall. It digs holes to catch Bug-type Pokémon."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"It lives in areas of limited rainfall. When danger approaches, it curls up into a ball to protect its soft stomach."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"When its skin gets wrinkled from moisture, it heads for a volcano. It lies flat on a spot with a lot of geothermal heat and dries itself out."},{"version":"sword","text":"It loves to bathe in the grit of dry, sandy areas. By sand bathing, the Pokémon rids itself of dirt and moisture clinging to its body."},{"version":"shield","text":"It burrows into the ground to create its nest. If hard stones impede its tunneling, it uses its sharp claws to shatter them and then carries on digging."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate